<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Explore interactive Bokeh examples across scientific computing, finance, operations, and exploratory analysis.">
  <title>Bokeh demos · Interactive data applications</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/bokeh-icon.svg?v=2" type="image/svg+xml" sizes="any">
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico?v=2" type="image/png" sizes="16x16">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css?v=13">
</head>
<body>
  {{ site_header | safe }}
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="hero-label">Bokeh example gallery</p>
          <h1>See what Bokeh can do.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">These examples use Bokeh for data exploration, scientific models, financial analysis, image processing, and network science. Each one has working source code.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="#demos">Browse the gallery</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://docs.bokeh.org/en/latest/">Bokeh documentation</a>
          </div>
          <div class="runtime-proof" aria-label="Runtime details">
            <span><b>{{ "%02d" | format(demos | length) }}</b> examples</span><span><b>Python / ASGI</b> current collection</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-index">
          <p>Jump to an example</p>
          <ol>
            {% for demo in demos %}
            <li><a href="{{ demo.route }}"><span>{{ "%02d" | format(loop.index) }}</span><b>{{ demo.title }}</b><small>{{ demo.domain }}</small></a></li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="gallery" id="demos">
      {% if show_legacy_notice %}
      <aside class="legacy-notice" role="status">
        <p>Demo site update</p>
        <div>
          <h2>The demo gallery has changed.</h2>
          <p>The example you followed belonged to the previous demo site and is no longer hosted here. Browse the new collection of richer Bokeh applications below.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="section-kicker"><span></span>Current collection</p><h2>Examples by topic</h2></div>
        <p>The gallery uses public datasets and computed models. Several examples also show how Bokeh works with NetworkX, Xarray, Numba, pandas, and scikit-image.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="demo-grid">
        {% for demo in demos %}
        <a class="demo-card accent-{{ demo.accent }}" href="{{ demo.route }}">
          <div class="demo-art" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="/assets/{{ demo.preview }}?v=11" alt="">
          </div>
          <div class="demo-copy">
            <div class="demo-meta"><span>{{ demo.domain }}</span><span>{{ demo.runtime }}</span></div>
            <h3>{{ demo.title }}</h3>
            <p>{{ demo.description }}</p>
            <ul>{% for tag in demo.tags %}<li>{{ tag }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
            <span class="open-demo">Open demo <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span>
          </div>
        </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="asgi-band" aria-label="Current runtime">
      <div class="asgi-band-inner">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker"><span></span>Current runtime</p>
          <h2>Python callbacks on ASGI</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="asgi-diagram" aria-label="Browser connects through an ASGI server to Bokeh and Python callbacks">
          <span><b>Browser</b><small>Document + WebSocket</small></span><i>→</i><span><b>ASGI server</b><small>Uvicorn today</small></span><i>→</i><span><b>Bokeh</b><small>Session + callbacks</small></span>
        </div>
        <p>Bokeh's ASGI adapter handles documents, static resources, sessions, and WebSockets. These examples run on Uvicorn, but the adapter can also sit inside another ASGI application.</p>
        <div class="run-local" id="run-locally">
          <div>
            <p class="run-local-label">Run locally</p>
            <h3>Clone it, then let uv do the rest.</h3>
            <p>With Git and <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">uv</a> installed, these commands create the locked environment and start the complete gallery.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/bokeh/demo.bokeh.org
cd demo.bokeh.org
uv run --locked uvicorn asgi:application</code></pre>
            <p>Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8000</code>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="runtime-section">
      <div class="runtime-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker"><span></span>Planned additions</p>
        <h2>The catalog also supports browser-only examples.</h2>
        <p>Each entry records both its domain and runtime. BokehJS, framework integrations, and browser-based Python examples can use the same gallery with accurate labels.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="runtime-grid">
        {% for runtime in runtime_roadmap %}
        <article class="runtime-card runtime-{{ runtime.accent }}">
          <span>{{ "%02d" | format(loop.index) }}</span>
          <p>{{ runtime.state }}</p>
          <h3>{{ runtime.title }}</h3>
          <div></div>
          <p>{{ runtime.description }}</p>
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  {{ site_footer | safe }}
</body>
</html>
